# invariant Remote HTTP bodies are untrusted text

Every non-success remote response rendered to a user goes through `ErrorResponse`. A body whose
trimmed form begins with `<`, or whose Content-Type is `text/html`, is never rendered; the error
reports only the HTTP status and `(html response, N bytes, suppressed)`. Other bodies have control
characters removed, whitespace collapsed, and their excerpt limited to 200 Unicode characters.
